cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "colombian-open-data-mcp: an MCP server for Colombia's open government data"
message: >-
  If you use this software, or figures obtained through it, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alberto
    family-names: Castillo Aroca
    alias: alcastaro
    affiliation: >-
      OLDS — Observatorio Latinoamericano de Desarrollo Sostenible
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/alcastaro/colombian-open-data-mcp"
url: "https://github.com/alcastaro/colombian-open-data-mcp"
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol server that turns Colombia's open government data
  into a native integration for any MCP client. It covers two portals on two
  different platforms: the national catalogue at datos.gov.co, which runs
  Socrata and is queried server-side with SoQL, and Bogotá's city catalogue at
  datosabiertos.bogota.gov.co, which runs CKAN and is queried through the
  DataStore. Because both platforms execute the query themselves, no local
  cache or download step is needed and only rolled-up results cross the wire.
  The differences between the two portals are exposed rather than smoothed
  over: Bogotá does not offer server-side aggregation, and the server declines
  to advertise one.
